# Keep api/'s test files out of the Vercel deployment bundle.
#
# Vercel turns every top-level file in api/ into a serverless function. A test
# file like api/payments.test.js would therefore be deployed as a function,
# consuming a slot against the Hobby-plan limit of 12 (we are already at 12) and
# potentially failing the build. Excluding them here means they are never
# uploaded, so they can never be mistaken for functions.
#
# Scoped to api/ only (not a blanket */.test.js): .vercelignore controls what
# Vercel's build container even sees, not just what gets deployed. A repo-wide
# pattern here also strips src/**/*.test.jsx and scripts/*.test.js before
# `vercel-build` ever runs `npm run test`, which then finds zero test files
# and fails the build. Only api/'s test files pose the function-count risk.
api/**/*.test.js
api/**/*.test.ts
api/**/*.spec.js
api/**/*.spec.ts
